    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0344" n="244" xml:id="pg244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/3335: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-03T11:00:00+01:00">August 3, 1934—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 3—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>163. Your 100, August 2, 11 a.m.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d207-f1"/> Hitler has
                    addressed letter to Minister of Interior stating that in view of association of
                    title of Reichs President with personality of Hindenburg, he shall continue to
                    be addressed as heretofore as Fuehrer and Chancellor. In the same communication
                    he expresses desire that the people should specifically sanction in free and
                    secret vote the entrusting of functions of former President to him and to office
                    of Chancellor which Cabinet had already decided. Accordingly 19th August has
                    been designated as voting day.</p>
                <p>In view of Schmitt illness Schacht designated Minister of Economics for 6 months.
                    Meissner designated to continue as head of the secretariat of the President.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
